# Themes

A theme names a strategic area the program serves for months to years:
the why behind the work. The technical program manager writes and owns
it. A theme is a direction, not a deliverable, so it is never done. Its
progress is the progress of the initiatives under it.

## Documents here

- Name: `thNNN-short-name.md`, numbered in order and never reused.
- Format: an SRD in the pinned parent release's Markdown format, with the fields docs/constitutions/design.md lists for this level; the draft skill drafts one in that layout.
- Status: `to_be_agreed` while it is drafted, `agreed` once it passes review, and `retired` when it is replaced. Only agreed documents are planned and rolled up. A retired document keeps its path, because links pin it.
- Parent: none. A theme is the top of the hierarchy, and initiatives name it as theirs.
- Changes go through an issue and the corpus gate, never a direct edit on main.

## What reads them

- Initiatives name a theme as their parent; a theme's progress is that of its initiatives.

See README.md at the repository's root for the whole hierarchy.
